// "glow" — a SHADER: picture in, picture out, and an optional audio input that drives it.
//
// The folder it sits in (`_modules/shaders/`) is what says so; nothing here names a plugin,
// because there is none. What this module DOES is the GLSL under `shaders/`, one folder per
// shader, and `shader:` below picks which of them runs.
//
// `P1`..`P4` are the four knobs every shader gets, 0..1, reaching the fragment as `uP1`..`uP4`.
// What each one means is the shader's business — read the comments in its fragment.glsl.
// See packages/song/docs/shaders.md.
type("shader")
shader("pulse")
params({
  P1: 0.6, // pulse: how hard the sound lifts the picture
  P2: 0.35, // pulse: vignette
  P3: 0,
  P4: 0,
})
